      "problem": "Factor $x^3 - 8.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\na^3-b^3=(a-b)(a^2+ab+b^2).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write the given expression as a difference of cubes:\n\n$$\nx^3 - 8 = x^3 - 2^3\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the given expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nx^3 - 8 & = x^3 - 2^3\\[3pt]\n\n& = (x - 2)\\left(x^2 + 2\\cdot x + 2^2\\right)\\[3pt]\n\n& = (x - 2)\\left(x^2 + 2x + 4\\right)\t\t\n\t}\n$$",
